---
/**
 * STUDENT-CENTRED LEARNING — the school seen from the learner's side.
 *
 * ═══ WHY THIS FILE WAS REBUILT ═════════════════════════════════════════════
 *
 * The first version was five sections that were all the same section: numeral,
 * eyebrow, heading, paragraph, photograph, alternating left and right. The
 * client's read of it was exact — the problem was not the content, it was that
 * the page had been assembled rather than composed.
 *
 * Every section here now has ONE dominant idea and its own composition rules:
 *
 *   HERO      photography + a display word at poster scale; a portrait breaks
 *             the section's bottom edge and lands in the next one
 *   POTENTIAL typography-led. The statement IS the section; one portrait
 *             overlaps the type and the prose sits small in the margin
 *   SAFE      immersive full-bleed. Three words over the photograph, no box
 *   VOICE     an overlapping collage on white; labels set bare, never in cards
 *   TOGETHER  panorama with a single word at poster scale across it
 *   MANY      an uneven orbit on a LIGHT ground, sizes and opacities varied,
 *             two satellites deliberately cropped by the section edge
 *   CLOSE     full-bleed, dark, one statement
 *
 * ⚠ NO SECTION NUMERALS, NO EYEBROW ON EVERY SECTION, NO ALTERNATING SPLIT, AND
 * NO SECTION SITTING IN A ROUNDED CARD. Those were the repeating parts.
 *
 * ⚠ COLOUR RHYTHM IS DELIBERATE, not decoration:
 *     ink → ivory → photograph → paper → photograph → sand → ink
 * The dark grounds are the two ends and one middle beat, so the page has a
 * shape rather than a texture.
 *
 * ⚠ THE ORBIT SITS ON SAND, NOT ON INK. The Teaching Philosophy page already
 * owns a dark constellation, and on ink the ornament PNGs — cap, bulb, saturn,
 * brush — are dark artwork that needs a light plate under every node to be seen
 * at all, which is what turned it into "centre circle + eight cards". On a light
 * ground the artwork reads unaided, so the plates are gone and the satellites
 * can vary in size and opacity the way an editorial orbit should.
 *
 * ═══ SOURCE OF TRUTH ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
 *
 *   /about-us/
 *     "Learn effectively and develop their full potential."
 *     "Ensure that all children receive equal regard and equal access to the
 *      curriculum."
 *     "Provide all children with a secure, caring, friendly and well-organized
 *      environment where discipline is consistent."
 *     "Incorporate Technology, a theory of Multiple Intelligence and
 *      Collaborative learning in all areas of teaching."
 *     "Develop in children a degree of independence and self-motivation."
 *
 *   /  (Principal Speak)
 *     "every child feels valued, safe, and inspired to achieve their full
 *      potential"
 *     "classrooms are places of curiosity and collaboration"
 *
 *   /principals-message/
 *     "all the students do not have the same talents and so each one will
 *      achieve success differently"
 *
 *   /event-chronicles-main/  (Children's Forum)
 *     "The forum provided a wonderful platform for students to express their
 *      thoughts, share their ideas, and engage in meaningful discussions on
 *      academics and school activities."
 *     "our students are not just learners but active contributors to the
 *      school's growth and progress"
 *
 * ⚠ WHAT WAS REMOVED AND WHY. An earlier version said students were "handling
 * the apparatus, reading the source, running the code, and defending a finding
 * to the group", and that "most of the talking in a lesson is done by students".
 * None of it appears anywhere on the school's site, so it is gone — from here
 * and from data/academicTopics.ts, which is where it actually lived.
 *
 * ⚠ "MULTIPLE INTELLIGENCE STATIONS" IS NOT CLAIMED. Searched About Us, the
 * homepage, the Principal's Message and both Event Chronicles pages — the phrase
 * is on none of them. The orbit is built on the About Us line, which is
 * verifiable, and on the Principal's own sentence about talents differing.
 *
 * ⚠ SCOPE. Teaching Philosophy, Curriculum, Experiential and Project work,
 * STEM, Robotics, AI, Smart Classrooms, Assessment, Careers, Structure and
 * Parent Partnership each have their own page. Where a theme overlaps, this page
 * takes the learner's half of it.
 *
 * ⚠ MOTION IS THE SITE'S OWN CONTRACT — data-split, data-reveal(+delay),
 * data-pop(+delay), data-parallax(+y), data-mask — handled by
 * scripts/motion-gsap.ts, already gated on prefers-reduced-motion and Save-Data.
 */
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';

/* ─── Photography ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Nine frames, every one opened and looked at before it was placed, and each
   given a DIFFERENT treatment: full bleed, cropped portrait, collage, panorama,
   circular mask. No frame is used twice. */

/* ─── Ornament ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Transparent PNGs already in the repository. Used at poster scale, bleeding off
   edges and sitting behind type — never as a glyph beside a heading. */
import dKite from '../../assets/icons/kite.png';
import dStars from '../../assets/icons/two-stars.png';
import dStar from '../../assets/icons/star.png';
import { getStudentCentredLearning } from '../../lib/cms';
import RichLine from '../ui/RichLine.astro';
import { fileUrl } from '../../lib/cms';
import SmartImage from '../ui/SmartImage.astro';


const scl = await getStudentCentredLearning();
const { one, two, three, close } = scl;

/**
 * The orbit.
 *
 * ⚠ POSITIONS ARE COMPUTED HERE, NOT BY A CSS TRANSFORM. An earlier
 * constellation used `transform: rotate(var(--a)) translate(...)`; the rule
 * shipped intact but computed to `none` and every node collapsed onto the
 * centre. Trigonometry at build time sidesteps it — each satellite gets a plain
 * left/top percentage and needs no counter-rotation to stay upright.
 *
 * `s` is a scale multiplier and `o` an opacity. Both vary per satellite on
 * purpose: a ring of identical chips at one radius is the generic version of
 * this idea, and it is what the first build shipped. Two satellites are placed
* placed in a 33–40% band. That band is not a style choice — it is what keeps
 * every satellite clear of the core circle at its inner edge and inside the
 * stage at its outer edge ONCE THE RING TURNS. Static, the first build got away
 * with 29–45%: each satellite sat at one angle and the tight ones happened to be
 * where nothing collided. Rotating carries every satellite through every angle,
 * so the worst case for one is now the worst case for all, and at 900–1024 the
 * inner ones were measured overlapping the core by up to 61px.
 */
/* ⚠ EACH WORD NAMES WHAT ITS ICON ACTUALLY SHOWS, and `s` BALANCES OPTICAL
 * WEIGHT RATHER THAN GEOMETRY. The set mixes two drawing styles the repository
 * happens to hold: thin outline art (pencil, bulb, brush) and bold filled
 * stickers with a dark keyline (questions, focus). At one size the stickers
 * shout and the outlines disappear, so the stickers are scaled DOWN and the
 * outlines UP until they carry the same weight on the page.
 *
 * The opacity floor is 0.85. The first pass ran down to 0.6 for depth, and two
 * satellites simply read as half-loaded images.
 *
 * ⚠ MOVEMENT IS A FULL ILLUSTRATION, NOT AN ICON — a figure striding up a stack
 * of books, roughly 1400px wide with a laptop and a bulb in it. At orbit size it
 * carries less detail than the single-object pieces beside it, which is why its
 * scale sits between the stickers and the outlines rather than at either end.
 *
 * Nine satellites now sit 40° apart rather than eight at 45°, so the set is
 * measurably tighter — the overlap assertion is what keeps that honest.
 *
 * Dropped earlier: the paper plane and the small figure — the two thinnest pieces of art
 * in the set, illegible at this size and the weakest match to their words. */
/**
 * ⚠ THE ANGLE IS COMPUTED, NOT STORED. The nine nodes sit at 10°, 50°, 90° … —
 * an even share of the circle with a 10° offset, so `10 + i × 360 / n`. It was
 * stored per card, which let an editor drag a node off the ring or add a tenth
 * that overlapped the first. The ring now re-spaces itself.
 */
const ORBIT_OFFSET = 10;

/**
 * ⚠ WHERE EACH NODE SITS, AND HOW BIG IT IS — DESIGN, NOT CONTENT.
 *
 * The angle is even (see above), but the radius, scale and opacity of each node
 * were placed by hand for balance: the ring alternates 34 and 40, and the sizes
 * vary so the constellation does not read as nine identical dots. None of it is
 * something an editor should be asked about, and none of it is derivable.
 *
 * ⚠ IT CYCLES. A tenth card added in the admin takes the first placement rather
 * than landing at the centre with no size at all.
 */
const ORBIT_PLACEMENT = [
  { r: 34, s: 1.1,  o: 1    }, { r: 40, s: 0.95, o: 0.88 }, { r: 34, s: 1.05, o: 0.96 },
  { r: 40, s: 0.8,  o: 0.9  }, { r: 33, s: 1.05, o: 1    }, { r: 40, s: 0.86, o: 0.94 },
  { r: 34, s: 1,    o: 0.9  }, { r: 40, s: 1,    o: 0.96 }, { r: 34, s: 0.78, o: 0.92 },
];
const placementOf = (i) => ORBIT_PLACEMENT[i % ORBIT_PLACEMENT.length];
const angleOf = (i) => ORBIT_OFFSET + (i * 360) / three.cards.length;

const at = (a: number, r: number) => ({
  x: (50 + r * Math.cos((a * Math.PI) / 180)).toFixed(2),
  y: (50 + r * Math.sin((a * Math.PI) / 180)).toFixed(2),
});
---

<div class="sc">
  {/* ═══ EVERY CHILD HAS POTENTIAL ══════════════════════════════════════════
      ⚠ THIS IS TEACHING PHILOSOPHY §01's COMPOSITION, AT THE CLIENT'S REQUEST.
      Copy column left — oversized numeral, eyebrow, statement, the Principal’s
      line as a rule-bordered quote, then the prose — and one large landscape
      frame right, on ivory with the drawn grid and the corner wash. The earlier
      typography-led version (statement at 132px across the full width, prose in
      the margin) is gone. */}
  <section class="sc-pot" aria-labelledby="sc-pot-h">
    <span class="sc__grid" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <span class="sc__wash" aria-hidden="true"></span>

    <div class="u-container sc-pot__in">
      <div class="sc-pot__copy">
        <p class="sc__n" aria-hidden="true">01</p>
        <p class="sc__k t-label" data-reveal>{one.kicker}</p>
        <h2 class="sc-pot__h" id="sc-pot-h" data-split>
          {one.heading} <em>{one.headingEm}</em>
        </h2>

        {/* ⚠ The curly quotes are typography and stay here — an editor types the
            sentence, the design sets the marks round it. */}
        <blockquote class="sc-quote" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="110">
          <p>“{one.quote}”</p>
          <cite>{one.quoteAuthor} · Principal</cite>
        </blockquote>

        <RichLine class="sc__p" text={one.body[0]} reveal revealDelay={200} />
      </div>

      <figure class="sc-pot__art" data-mask data-zoom>
        <SmartImage
          file={one.image}
          alt={one.imageAlt}
         
          widths={[520, 900]}
          sizes="(max-width: 900px) 92vw, 46vw"
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
        />
      </figure>
    </div>

    <img class="sc__f sc__f--kite" src={dKite.src} alt="" aria-hidden="true" data-parallax data-parallax-y="56" />
    <img class="sc__f sc__f--sparks" src={dStars.src} alt="" aria-hidden="true" />
  </section>

  {/* ═══ OUR VOICE MATTERS ══════════════════════════════════════════════════
      A collage on paper. One large frame, two smaller ones tucked behind it at
      opposing angles, and the labels set bare against the white. */}
  <section class="sc-voice" aria-labelledby="sc-voice-h">
    {/* Ghost typography — the section's subject set at poster scale and almost no
        contrast, bleeding off the left edge. Decorative, so it is hidden from the
        accessibility tree and cannot be selected. */}
    <span class="sc-voice__ghost" aria-hidden="true">Forum</span>

    <div class="u-container sc-voice__in">
      <div class="sc-voice__lede">
        <h2 class="sc-voice__h" id="sc-voice-h" data-split>{two.heading}<br />{two.headingSecond}</h2>

        {/* The three words used to float in the gutter between the copy and the
            photographs, hung off nothing and spread over 700px of empty white.
            As a rule-separated index line under the headline they support it
            instead of drifting beside it. */}
        <ul class="sc-voice__index" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="90">
          {two.index.map((w) => <li>{w}</li>)}
        </ul>

        <RichLine class="sc-voice__p" text={two.body[0]} reveal revealDelay={150} />
        <RichLine class="sc-voice__pull" text={two.body[1]} reveal revealDelay={230} />
      </div>

      <div class="sc-voice__collage">
        <figure class="sc-voice__a" data-mask data-zoom>
          <SmartImage
            file={two.imageOne}
            alt={two.imageOneAlt}
           
            widths={[420, 900]}
            sizes="(max-width: 900px) 86vw, 40vw"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </figure>

        {/* A circle, not a tilted rectangle. The old second frame was a rotated
            crop of a torso peeping from behind the first — it read as a mistake
            rather than as a layer. */}
        <figure class="sc-voice__b" data-pop data-pop-delay="140" data-zoom data-zoom-to="1.16">
          <SmartImage
            file={two.imageTwo}
            alt={two.imageTwoAlt}
           
            widths={[300, 620]}
            sizes="(max-width: 900px) 40vw, 18vw"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </figure>

        <figure class="sc-voice__c" data-pop data-pop-delay="230" data-zoom>
          <SmartImage
            file={two.imageThree}
            alt={two.imageThreeAlt}
           
            widths={[280, 560]}
            sizes="(max-width: 900px) 38vw, 16vw"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>

    <img class="sc__f sc__f--stars" src={dStars.src} alt="" aria-hidden="true" />
  </section>

  {/* ═══ ONE LEARNER → MANY POSSIBILITIES ═══════════════════════════════════
      The signature. A light ground so the ornament reads without a plate under
      every node, satellites at varying scale and opacity, and two of them cropped
      by the section edge. */}
  <section class="sc-many" aria-labelledby="sc-many-h">
    <div class="u-container sc-many__in">
      <div class="sc-many__copy">
        <h2 class="sc-many__h" id="sc-many-h" data-split>
          {three.heading}<br /><em>{three.headingEm}</em>
        </h2>
        <RichLine class="sc-many__p" text={three.body[0]} reveal revealDelay={140} />
        <RichLine class="sc-many__foot" text={three.body[1]} reveal revealDelay={220} />
      </div>

      <div class="sc-eco" data-reveal>
      <div class="sc-eco__core" data-zoom data-zoom-to="1.08">
        <SmartImage
          file={three.image}
          alt={three.imageAlt}
         
          widths={[360, 719]}
          sizes="(max-width: 700px) 56vw, 320px"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
      </div>

      <svg class="sc-eco__lines" viewBox="0 0 400 400" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
        <circle cx="200" cy="200" r="132" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="1.5 13" />
        <circle cx="200" cy="200" r="160" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="1.5 13" />
      </svg>

      <ul class="sc-eco__set">
        {
          three.cards.map((n, i) => {
            const place = placementOf(i);
            const p = at(angleOf(i), place.r);
            /* ⚠ NO data-pop ON THESE, DELIBERATELY. ScrollTrigger caches an
               element's position when it refreshes, and these are moved
               continuously by the orbit rotation — so the cached trigger points
               go stale and satellites that have already scrolled into view never
               fire. Measured: three of the eight sat on screen at opacity 0 and
               only appeared after another 400px of scrolling. The stage as a
               whole carries `data-reveal`, which is one trigger on one element
               that does not move. */
            return (
              <li
                class="sat"
                style={`--x: ${p.x}%; --y: ${p.y}%; --s: ${place.s}; --o: ${place.o};`}
              >
                {/* ⚠ <Image>, NOT <img src={art.src}>. The raw files are
                    920KB, 260KB and 235KB — served unprocessed that is well over
                    a megabyte of ornament on a page whose photographs are
                    already optimised. Astro emits a ~120px webp instead. */}
                <SmartImage
                  file={n.icon}
                  alt=""
                  fallbackWidth={1100}
                />
                <span class="sat__k">{n.label}</span>
              </li>
            );
          })
        }
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <img class="sc__f sc__f--star" src={dStar.src} alt="" aria-hidden="true" />
  </section>

  {/* ═══ CLOSE ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */}
  <section class="sc-end" aria-labelledby="sc-end-h">
    <figure class="sc-end__art" data-zoom data-zoom-to="1.1">
      <SmartImage
        file={close.image}
        alt={close.imageAlt}
       
        widths={[900, 1400, 1920]}
        sizes="100vw"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
    </figure>
    <span class="sc-end__scrim" aria-hidden="true"></span>

    <div class="u-container sc-end__in">
      <h2 class="sc-end__h" id="sc-end-h" data-split>
      {/* Any number of lines: the page puts the breaks in and sets the
          last one in italic. Three lines on one page, two on another. */}
      {close.headingLines.map((line, i) => (
        <>{i > 0 && <br />}{i === close.headingLines.length - 1 ? <em>{line}</em> : line}</>
      ))}
      </h2>
      <p class="sc-end__p" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="120">
        {close.quote}
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<style>
  .sc { position: relative; }

  /* Ornament. `pointer-events: none` throughout — decoration must never swallow
     a click meant for the copy under it. */
  .sc__f {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 3;
    pointer-events: none;
    user-select: none;
  }

  /* ⚠ EVERY FRAME STRETCHES ITS <picture>, NOT JUST ITS <img>. astro:assets
     emits <picture><img></picture> and <picture> is an INLINE box, so it takes
     its intrinsic height and an img's `height: 100%` resolves against that
     rather than against the figure. On any frame with a declared aspect-ratio or
     an absolute fill, the photo comes up short of its own box. */
  .sc :global(figure > picture) { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; }

  /* ═══ POTENTIAL ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     Teaching Philosophy §01's composition: copy left, one large frame right, on
     ivory with a drawn grid and a corner wash. */
  .sc-pot {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    padding-block: clamp(52px, 8vw, 108px);
    background: var(--sb-ivory);
  }

  .sc-pot__in {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(30px, 4.6vw, 66px);
    align-items: center;
  }

  /* ⚠ ORNAMENT, SO aria-hidden AND NOT A HEADING. A screen reader announcing
     "zero one" before the section adds nothing the heading level does not
     already carry. */
  .sc__n {
    font-family: var(--sb-font-display);
    font-size: clamp(44px, 6vw, 92px);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 0.82;
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
    color: rgba(201, 60, 10, 0.16);
  }

  .sc__k { margin-top: var(--sb-3); color: var(--sb-violet-dark); }

  .sc-pot__h {
    margin-top: var(--sb-3);
    font-family: var(--sb-font-display);
    font-size: clamp(32px, 4.8vw, 62px);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.02;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    color: var(--sb-charcoal);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .sc-pot__h em { font-style: normal; color: var(--sb-violet); }

  .sc-quote {
    margin: clamp(16px, 2vw, 22px) 0 0;
    padding-left: clamp(16px, 2vw, 22px);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--sb-violet);
  }
  .sc-quote p {
    font-family: var(--sb-font-display);
    font-size: clamp(17px, 1.7vw, 24px);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.42;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--sb-charcoal);
  }
  .sc-quote cite {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 9px;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--sb-violet-dark);
  }

  :global(.sc__p) {
    max-width: 54ch;
    margin-top: clamp(16px, 2vw, 22px);
    font-size: clamp(15px, 1.1vw, 17px);
    line-height: 1.76;
    color: var(--sb-text-secondary);
  }
  :global(.sc__p strong) { font-weight: 700; color: var(--sb-charcoal); }

  .sc-pot__art {
    margin: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    border-radius: var(--sb-r-3);
    box-shadow: 0 40px 80px -46px rgba(27, 21, 18, 0.6);
  }
  .sc-pot__art :global(img) { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; }

  /* Backgrounds — drawn, never downloaded. */
  .sc__grid,
  .sc__wash { position: absolute; z-index: 0; pointer-events: none; }

  .sc__grid {
    inset: 0;
    background-image:
      linear-gradient(to right, rgba(27, 21, 18, 0.045) 1px, transparent 1px),
      linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(27, 21, 18, 0.045) 1px, transparent 1px);
    background-size: 76px 76px;
    -webkit-mask-image: radial-gradient(78% 70% at 26% 22%, #000, transparent 76%);
    mask-image: radial-gradient(78% 70% at 26% 22%, #000, transparent 76%);
  }

  .sc__wash {
    top: -14%;
    right: -8%;
    width: min(46vw, 620px);
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    border-radius: 50%;
    filter: blur(20px);
    background: radial-gradient(circle, rgba(201, 60, 10, 0.16) 0%, rgba(201, 60, 10, 0) 68%);
  }

  .sc__f--kite { top: 5%; right: 4%; width: clamp(52px, 6.5vw, 100px); }
  .sc__f--sparks { top: 8%; right: 22%; width: clamp(30px, 3.6vw, 56px); opacity: 0.8; }

  /* ═══ VOICE ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     A cluster on paper — the page's only pure-white ground, which is what makes
     the overlap and the circular mask read. */
  .sc-voice {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    padding-block: clamp(64px, 10vw, 144px);
    background: var(--sb-paper);
  }

  /* Set at poster scale, bled off the left edge, and pushed almost to the
     ground's own value so it is felt rather than read. */
  .sc-voice__ghost {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    left: -0.06em;
    z-index: 0;
    translate: 0 -50%;
    font-family: var(--sb-font-display);
    font-size: clamp(180px, 30vw, 460px);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 0.8;
    letter-spacing: -0.06em;
    color: rgba(27, 21, 18, 0.035);
    pointer-events: none;
    user-select: none;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .sc-voice__in {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(34px, 5vw, 64px);
    align-items: center;
  }

  .sc-voice__h {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--sb-font-display);
    font-size: clamp(36px, 7vw, 92px);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 0.92;
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
    color: var(--sb-charcoal);
  }

  /* The index line. Tracked caps with a hairline rule between them — the three
     words now brace the headline instead of floating in the gutter. */
  .sc-voice__index {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px 14px;
    margin: clamp(18px, 2.4vw, 26px) 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .sc-voice__index li {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 14px;
    font-size: 11.5px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--sb-violet-dark);
  }
  .sc-voice__index li + li::before {
    content: '';
    width: clamp(16px, 2vw, 30px);
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--sb-border-strong);
  }

  :global(.sc-voice__p) {
    max-width: 46ch;
